<section class="ref-group"><h2>Battles <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-strasbourg"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Strasbourg</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 357</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Strasbourg, or Argentoratum, was fought in August 357 near Strasbourg between a Roman army under the Caesar Julian and a coalition of Alemannic kings led…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-solicinium"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-solicinium.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Solicinium</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 368</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Solicinium was fought in 368 between the Roman army of Valentinian I and his young son Gratian and the Alemanni, at a hill site in south-west Germany…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fangtou"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Fangtou</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 369</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Fangtou was fought in 369 in northern China, when the Former Yan general Murong Chui defeated the northern expedition of the Eastern Jin commander Huan…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-adrianople"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-adrianople.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Adrianople</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 378 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Adrianople was fought in 378 CE in Thrace between the Roman army under the eastern emperor Valens and Gothic forces.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-argentovaria"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Argentovaria</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 378</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Argentovaria was fought in 378 in Alsace between the Western Roman army of the emperor Gratian and the Alemannic Lentienses, who had crossed the frozen…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fei-river"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-fei-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Fei River</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 383</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Fei River was fought in 383 in present-day Anhui, where a much smaller Eastern Jin army under Xie Xuan, directed by Xie An, routed the invading force of…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-frigidus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-frigidus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of the Frigidus</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 394</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of the Frigidus was fought on 5–6 September 394 by the river Frigidus, probably the Vipava in present-day Slovenia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-canhe-slope"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-canhe-slope.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Battle of Canhe Slope</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · 395</span><span class="enc-snip">The Battle of Canhe Slope was fought in 395 in northern China between the Later Yan army of Murong Bao and the forces of Tuoba Gui of Northern Wei.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Sieges <span class="n">1</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-amida-359"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Amida (359)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 359 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Amida in 359 CE was the capture of the Roman city of Amida, modern Diyarbakir, by the Sasanian king Shapur II.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Wars &amp; campaigns <span class="n">2</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-conquest-of-kush"><span class="enc-name">Aksumite conquest of Kush</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · c. 350 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aksumite conquest of Kush was the campaign led by the Aksumite king Ezana around c. 350 CE against the Kingdom of Kush and its centre at Meroë.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/gothic-war-376-382"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/gothic-war-376-382.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Gothic War (376–382)</span><span class="enc-type">War · 376–382</span><span class="enc-snip">The Gothic War of 376–382 was fought between the Roman Empire and Gothic groups, chiefly the Tervingi and Greuthungi, who had crossed the Danube fleeing the Huns.</span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="ref-group"><h2>Treaties <span class="n">1</span></h2><ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-363"><span class="enc-name">Peace of 363</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 363 CE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Peace of 363 was the treaty concluded in 363 CE between Rome and the Sasanian Empire after the Roman emperor Julian died during his invasion of Persia.</span></a></li></ul></section>
